sequenceDiagram
    accTitle: GitLab sync and mesh execution
    accDescr: CI requests sync over SSH. The controller fetches once and returns a receipt. After manual release it verifies the staged project and dispatches signed work over the node's established outbound mTLS connection.
    participant J as GitLab CI jobs
    participant C as Controller
    participant G as Git repository
    participant I as Mesh ingress
    participant N as Execution node
    participant T as Target
    N->>I: Open outbound mTLS connection
    J->>C: Sync exact commit over pinned SSH
    C->>G: Fetch using read-only token
    G-->>C: Project at requested SHA
    C->>C: Stage project and record receipt
    C-->>J: Sync receipt and status
    Note over J,C: Operator reviews receipt and releases deploy
    J->>C: Execute synced request over SSH
    C->>C: Verify snapshot and claim execution
    C->>I: Submit signed work through local socket
    I-->>N: Deliver work over established connection
    N->>T: Run Ansible over SSH or WinRM
    T-->>N: Task results
    N-->>I: Stream execution results
    I-->>C: Record result and mesh UUID
    C-->>J: Return exit code
    J->>C: Retrieve original result archive
    C-->>J: Metadata and result files
